        "citation": "For the invention and development of the optical lattice clock."
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B011",
    "B005"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "Optical lattice clocks use controlled atomic motion and light to reach exceptional frequency precision. This is more than an improvement in timekeeping: it enables comparisons that test fundamental physics and makes the clock itself a precise probe of nature. Katori's lattice-clock concept and Ye's experimental realization and refinement form a clear, complementary contribution. Independent development and sustained advances across laboratories show that the result is robust and scientifically mature.",
    "case_against": "The clock field has many contributors, and the boundary between the original lattice-clock achievement and later advances in optical frequency standards needs careful historical review. The technology's continuing evolution also makes it difficult to choose a single milestone as the prize's endpoint.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson supports Katori and Ye, while noting that the broader clock community's contributions deserve careful review.",
        "response": "I agree that the history must be examined closely. The two names represent distinct, central steps in the lattice-clock achievement; recognizing those steps need not imply that they alone advanced every part of optical clock science."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson notes that international adoption as a time standard remains a longer process and asks how to weigh the original concept against later precision engineering.",
        "response": "Adoption as a standard is not the right measure of the physics achievement. The clock's demonstrated precision and its use in fundamental tests already establish its scientific importance. The citation should focus on the lattice-clock invention and development, while attribution review distinguishes that contribution from later improvements."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "The historical boundary between the foundational lattice-clock work and later advances in optical frequency standards needs review."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
